---
const more = [
  { href: '/portfolio/volunteer-scheduling-system/', label: 'Volunteer scheduling system' },
  { href: '/portfolio/contractor-website-lead-capture/', label: 'Contractor website' },
  { href: '/portfolio/fintech-integration-platform/', label: 'Fintech integration platform' },
];
---

<section id="case-study">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Proof of work</div>
      <h2 class="title title--section">One system, running unattended since early 2026</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="case-card">
      <p class="case-lead">A 200+ member church was burning staff hours every week on the same routine: turning each service's recording into a formatted outline document, updating two websites, organizing videos, assembling announcements, and getting it all in front of the congregation. Twice a week, every week — and when the one person who knew the process was busy, things slipped. I built a system that does the whole routine on its own.</p>

      <div class="case-stats">
        <div class="case-metric">
          <div class="stat">0 hrs</div>
          <div class="case-metric-label">Manual work per week</div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-metric">
          <div class="stat">40+</div>
          <div class="case-metric-label">Subscribers in week 1</div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-metric">
          <div class="stat">~1 hr</div>
          <div class="case-metric-label">Monthly maintenance</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="case-result">
        <div class="eyebrow">The result</div>
        <p>What previously consumed hours of staff time each week now runs entirely on its own. It's been in production since early 2026 and hasn't missed a service. It checks itself — I look at it about once a month. The staff stopped thinking about it, which was the whole point.</p>
        <p>The one place a human still touches the process is the one place a human should: nothing goes out to the congregation without a person approving it. Everything else runs unattended.</p>
      </div>

      <a class="btn btn--link" href="/portfolio/church-automation-pipeline/">Read the full case study — with the system diagram &rarr;</a>
    </div>

    <p class="case-more">
      <span class="case-more-label">More work:</span>
      {more.map((m, i) => (
        <Fragment>{i > 0 && <span class="case-sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span>}<a href={m.href}>{m.label}</a></Fragment>
      ))}
      <span class="case-sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="case-all" href="/portfolio/">All work →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .case-card {
    max-width: 52rem; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl); padding: clamp(var(--space-6), 4vw, var(--space-10));
  }
  .case-lead { font-size: var(--text-base); color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 60ch; }
  .case-stats {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-6) var(--space-12);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0; padding: var(--space-6) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .case-metric-label { font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .case-result { max-width: 60ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .case-result p { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .case-result p + p { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .case-more { margin-top: var(--space-6); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 52rem; }
  .case-more a { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
  .case-more a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .case-more-label { color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-right: var(--space-1); }
</style>
